<h1>Extract from Boundaries</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polylines &gt; Extract From Boundaries</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Extract From Boundaries</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command creates a polylines from visible selected mesh boundaries. All polylines created by this method will be placed in separate group. This command is grayed if there is no mesh selection or all selections are hidden.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP163632497" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image027.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs8">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image029.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: If the selected mesh contains holes, polylines will be extracted from their boundaries also. If you do not need them, use</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command">Select Polylines</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command to select and delete such polylines.</span></p>
